Description: Cinnamon clock with multiple time and calendar systems
 Calendar integrates with Cinnamon's panel, popup, settings and calendar
 service while adding French Republican decimal, Internet, Unix, hexadecimal,
 binary, sidereal, solar, Julian Date, mean-solar, Modified Julian, traditional
 Chinese, Roman temporal, Edo Japanese, Italian, Babylonian-hour, Indian ghaṭī
 Chinese hundred-kè and Nuremberg clock modes plus 30 civil, religious, historical
 and experimental calendar systems.
 .
 A platform-neutral C core handles conversion, grid construction, event
 intervals and precise scheduling. Thin native and JavaScript adapters provide
 Cinnamon integration. The same amd64 package can use the system ICU supplied
 by Ubuntu/Mint or Debian.
